# elohim/holochain/tests/sweettest — DNA integration tests

Sweettest scenarios exercising the elohim DNAs across one or more in-process conductors. This
manifest CLAIMS full responsibility for the subtree (`covers: subtree`); the `src/tests/` scenarios
inherit it.

## Unique-content-id invariant (edit-time advisory)

**Retries share the process-global mem-bootstrap store; fixed ids self-poison retries.** nextest
runs its RETRIES in the same OS process, and the kitsune2 mem-bootstrap DHT store is process-global.
A `create_content` call carrying a fixed string id means a retry re-joins the first attempt's DHT
residue, and the coordinator refuses the duplicate with "already exists" — so a scenario that fixed
its ids can never recover on retry (dna #1357). This is the bonus instance of defect class #5 in the
five-defect convergence arc: a test mechanism that breaks its own retry path. The cure is
`unique_id("base")` (epoch-nanos suffix, defined in `tests/lamad.rs`) per invocation — fresh ids
every attempt, byte-identical scenario.

The `unique-content-id-in-tests` rule fires as an advisory (class stays `inject` because
`epr:validator-sweettest-unique-content-id` is not registered in v1) when a `.rs` write in this
subtree calls `create_content` / `test_content(...)`. It surfaces the discipline at edit time
without blocking legitimate edits — single-agent tests with no retry-visible DHT residue may keep a
fixed id, but any multi-conductor or gossip-visible id should route through `unique_id()`.

See: `genesis/docs/content/elohim-protocol/history/2026-07-12-substrate-convergence-five-defect-arc.md`
